From 53cc67466cd5405128e9292d4644498446946c61 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:44:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Keep pytest-django's test groups under --det

detpy undid every reordering made in pytest_collection_modifyitems,
including pytest-django's: TestCase tests first, then transactional tests
(TransactionTestCase, transaction=True), then non-db tests. A transactional
test flushes the database, so TestCase tests collected after it lost the
rows created by data migrations and failed only under --det.

detpy now calls pytest-django's own hook (a stable sort) on its fixed or
seeded order: the group order is kept as a constraint and detpy's order is
kept inside each group. The result is a pure function of detpy's order, so
it stays deterministic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01YAF6Dgp7MTxUYBRZseFL3V
